{"author":{"id":"2de4467f26c42fb223f4d3ddd5611e7c0513d3daae4c1dc315de039036bc997d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778952300,"nonce":"KSKCG6sYHKa6rEt37p1U5aD/cIk=","title":"Harden diff mode command execution","message":"## Problem\nDiff mode shells out to git using string interpolation with values that can come from route/query state.\n\nExamples:\n- `getVersionAtCommit(filePath, commitSha)` builds `git show ${commitSha}:\\\"${relativePath}\\\"` with `execSync`.\n- Other git commands interpolate paths into shell strings.\n\n## Context\nDiff mode is disabled for normal static export, but it is explicitly supported by `ENABLE_DIFF` / `ENABLE_EDIT`. It is a local/editor-facing tool, so the right bar is not public-web hardening but local command hygiene: avoid letting malformed query parameters or paths become shell syntax.\n\n## Potential Solutions\n- Validate commit SHAs against a strict ref/SHA allowlist before use.\n- Use `execFileSync`/`spawnSync` with argv arrays instead of shell command strings.\n- Keep file paths resolved under the intended content root or current git root.\n- Add tests for rejected `diff` query values containing shell metacharacters.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}